The Thatch host on Scratch Everywhere!
======================================

The files in this directory are under two licenses. Every file says which one applies to it in a
line that starts with "SPDX-License-Identifier:", in the file itself or, where the format has no
comments, in a file of the same name with ".license" added.

1. The GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3

   ScratchEverywhere/
       Scratch Everywhere! (https://github.com/ScratchEverywhere/ScratchEverywhere), pinned as a
       git submodule. It is the work of its contributors and is licensed under the GNU Lesser
       General Public License, version 3 (SPDX: LGPL-3.0-only). Its license text is
       ScratchEverywhere/LICENSE, which builds on the GNU General Public License, version 3.

   patches/
       Changes to Scratch Everywhere!. A patch modifies the library, so it is under the library's
       license: the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3 or any later version
       (SPDX: LGPL-3.0-or-later).

2. The Apache License 2.0 with LLVM exceptions, the license of the rest of Thatch

   Everything else here: adapter/, tests/, CMakeLists.txt, README.md and this file
   (SPDX: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception). The license text is ../../LICENSE.

   The adapter is the program that uses the library. It includes the library's headers and calls
   its functions, and it contains no code copied from the library.

Nothing outside this directory is derived from, includes or depends on anything inside it, and
tools/check-hosts.sh, which CI runs, keeps it that way. This directory is not part of the Cargo
workspace and is never published to crates.io.

What this means for a game built with this host is described in docs/scratch-everywhere.md: the
game's own code can be under any license, and the library ships next to it as a shared library
that whoever gets the game can replace.
